WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.948
Module six, the last module. Account controls, staff logins, the vendor profile, and

2
00:00:05.948 --> 00:00:07.541
What is still being built.

3
00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:14.603
This last module is about control. Who can log in, who can do what, and what happens

4
00:00:14.603 --> 00:00:16.922
When something goes wrong with a vendor.

5
00:00:17.372 --> 00:00:21.148
First, the three admin actions: suspend, block and delete.

6
00:00:21.598 --> 00:00:24.158
Then what a suspended vendor can and can't do.

7
00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:25.910
Then the settings page.

8
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.816
Then creating a staff login, with permissions and warehouse scope.

9
00:00:30.266 --> 00:00:31.716
Then the vendor profile.

10
00:00:32.166 --> 00:00:34.044
And finally, what's still pending.

11
00:00:36.433 --> 00:00:39.071
The admin has three actions on a vendor account.

12
00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:41.489
They are very different, so learn them well.

13
00:00:41.939 --> 00:00:47.297
Suspend puts the vendor in read only mode. They can still log in, view their data

14
00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:52.523
And export it. But they cannot add S K Us, cannot receive new orders, and their

15
00:00:52.523 --> 00:00:58.080
Listings are hidden from buyers. To restore, the admin re-approves the vendor in the

16
00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.006
KYC lifecycle.

17
00:00:59.456 --> 00:01:02.730
Block is stronger. The vendor cannot log in at all.

18
00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:06.389
Use it for serious problems. The admin can unblock later.

19
00:01:06.839 --> 00:01:10.449
Delete removes the vendor account. It is the last resort.

20
00:01:10.449 --> 00:01:12.919
Think twice, because it's hard to undo.

21
00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:17.253
Let's watch this in the live demo.

22
00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:24.022
Here's the vendor, working normally, with Add S K U available.

23
00:01:29.867 --> 00:01:34.667
In the admin panel, Warehouses and Vendors, the admin searches for this vendor.

24
00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:48.022
The actions column has icons for view, change requests, suspend, block and delete.

25
00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:57.334
Hovering shows each label. This one is block.

26
00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:10.359
The admin clicks suspend. The dialog explains: the vendor will be switched to read

27
00:02:10.359 --> 00:02:15.716
Only mode. They can view the dashboard and export data, but cannot create or change

28
00:02:15.716 --> 00:02:17.782
Products, warehouses or pricing.

29
00:02:18.382 --> 00:02:23.310
Confirmed. The vendor disappears from the approved list, because it's now suspended.

30
00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:30.187
Let's watch this in the live demo.

31
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.786
On the vendor side, a yellow banner appears on every page: account suspended, read

32
00:02:37.786 --> 00:02:38.431
Only mode.

33
00:02:39.031 --> 00:02:43.383
The Add S K U button is gone. Product listings are hidden from buyers.

34
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.840
Orders can still be viewed and exported, but no new orders come in.

35
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.803
Even settings change for a suspended vendor.

36
00:02:56.253 --> 00:02:58.365
The read only banner stays at the top.

37
00:02:58.815 --> 00:03:02.667
And password updates are disabled while the account is suspended.

38
00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:06.281
When the admin re-approves the vendor, everything comes back.

39
00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:11.817
Remember: suspend is reversible, delete is not.

40
00:03:11.817 --> 00:03:17.246
Use suspend for a temporary problem, like expired documents, dues not cleared, or

41
00:03:17.246 --> 00:03:20.999
Complaints under review. Use block for serious problems.

42
00:03:20.999 --> 00:03:25.222
And delete only as a last resort, after checking with a senior.

43
00:04:00.833 --> 00:04:03.820
Now the vendor's settings page. It has three tabs.

44
00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:09.241
Password reset. Since the vendor is already logged in, no O T P is needed.

45
00:04:09.241 --> 00:04:11.928
Current password, new password, confirm.

46
00:04:12.378 --> 00:04:14.554
Staff, where staff logins are created.

47
00:04:15.004 --> 00:04:18.610
Privacy and data, to export data or request deletion.

48
00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.660
And the change password button.

49
00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:28.004
When creating a staff login, the main vendor ticks exactly which areas that person

50
00:04:28.004 --> 00:04:28.486
Can use.

51
00:04:28.936 --> 00:04:32.306
Inventory and listings: products, stock and pricing.

52
00:04:32.756 --> 00:04:36.554
Order management: view, accept, update status and dispatch.

53
00:04:37.004 --> 00:04:38.241
Drivers and fleet.

54
00:04:38.691 --> 00:04:42.339
E-way bills, warehouse management, and adding new warehouses.

55
00:04:42.789 --> 00:04:44.197
Disputes and returns.

56
00:04:44.647 --> 00:04:49.108
And account and compliance: viewing or updating KYC documents.

57
00:04:49.108 --> 00:04:53.714
Then the warehouse scope: all warehouses, or only selected ones.

58
00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.020
Let's watch this in the live demo.

59
00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:05.613
In the live demo, the vendor opens Settings, then the Staff tab, and clicks Add

60
00:05:05.613 --> 00:05:05.961
Staff.

61
00:05:11.433 --> 00:05:16.652
The form asks for full name, email, a ten digit mobile number, and a password of at

62
00:05:16.652 --> 00:05:19.796
Least six characters. We've blurred these details.

63
00:05:20.396 --> 00:05:25.693
Then the permissions. Here, inventory and listings, and order management are ticked.

64
00:05:25.693 --> 00:05:27.585
Drivers and fleet is left off.

65
00:05:31.433 --> 00:05:36.790
Scrolling down shows more groups: e-way bills, warehouse management, disputes and

66
00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:38.046
Returns, and K Y C.

67
00:05:47.433 --> 00:05:52.647
Warehouse access scope. Instead of all warehouses, selected warehouses is chosen,

68
00:05:52.647 --> 00:05:54.900
And only two warehouses are picked.

69
00:05:59.433 --> 00:06:02.270
Create sub admin. The staff account is saved.

70
00:06:31.433 --> 00:06:36.295
The staff accounts list shows each person, their number of modules, warehouse scope,

71
00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.494
An active toggle, and edit and delete.

72
00:06:47.433 --> 00:06:52.332
A second staff member is added the same way, with inventory and order management

73
00:06:52.332 --> 00:06:52.638
Only.

74
00:07:31.433 --> 00:07:36.213
Now there are two staff accounts. The active toggle can switch a login off at any

75
00:07:36.213 --> 00:07:37.748
Time, without deleting it.

76
00:07:39.543 --> 00:07:42.252
Here's what that staff member sees after logging in.

77
00:07:42.702 --> 00:07:47.630
The left menu has only the allowed sections: dashboard, inventory, orders and

78
00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.206
Settings.

79
00:07:48.656 --> 00:07:53.094
Settings has no staff tab, only password reset, and privacy and data.

80
00:07:53.544 --> 00:07:58.322
Under privacy and data, export my data as a multi page Excel file.

81
00:07:58.772 --> 00:08:04.472
And request data deletion. This is governed by India's D P D P Act twenty twenty

82
00:08:04.472 --> 00:08:10.314
Three. Settlement and G S T records are kept for eight years, as the law requires.

83
00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:17.809
One agreed change. Right now a staff login still shows the dashboard, with sales

84
00:08:17.809 --> 00:08:23.162
Figures. In the session it was agreed to remove the dashboard and sales numbers from

85
00:08:23.162 --> 00:08:27.241
Staff logins, so sensitive business figures stay with the owner.

86
00:08:27.241 --> 00:08:31.129
Also remember: only the vendor's main login can create users.

87
00:08:31.129 --> 00:08:33.169
Staff cannot create other staff.

88
00:09:19.043 --> 00:09:21.048
A few good habits for staff logins.

89
00:09:21.498 --> 00:09:26.768
One login per person. Never share a login, so every action can be traced to someone.

90
00:09:27.218 --> 00:09:31.420
Give only the permissions the job needs. A packer doesn't need earnings.

91
00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:35.262
Limit each person to the warehouses they actually work at.

92
00:09:35.712 --> 00:09:38.742
When someone leaves, switch off their toggle the same day.

93
00:09:39.192 --> 00:09:42.200
And the main login password stays with the owner only.

94
00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:48.663
The vendor profile, opened from the top right, has two kinds of fields.

95
00:09:49.113 --> 00:09:55.152
Locked fields, set by the KYC approval: the name and entity name, and the G S T I N.

96
00:09:55.152 --> 00:10:00.976
The vendor cannot edit these. If they must change, it goes back through the admin

97
00:10:00.976 --> 00:10:01.551
And KYC.

98
00:10:02.001 --> 00:10:05.874
Editable fields: the registered address, email and phone number.

99
00:10:05.874 --> 00:10:10.896
Keep the phone number real and working, because WhatsApp pickup slots and alerts go

100
00:10:10.896 --> 00:10:11.259
There.

101
00:10:13.643 --> 00:10:17.370
As of the eighteenth of November, these items were still pending.

102
00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:19.894
Some may be done by the time you watch this.

103
00:10:20.344 --> 00:10:24.632
An instant or express delivery option, checking Porter and other partners.

104
00:10:25.082 --> 00:10:29.476
An admin alert when a warehouse is added, with the verify then approve flow.

105
00:10:29.926 --> 00:10:32.486
Clearer Shiprocket error messages for vendors.

106
00:10:32.936 --> 00:10:36.350
Removing the dashboard and sales numbers from staff logins.

107
00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.957
The mobile app logo, which looks cropped on some phones.

108
00:10:40.407 --> 00:10:45.365
And re-submitting the app to the Apple App Store, after fixing the privacy policy.

109
00:10:45.365 --> 00:10:49.538
Google Play updates usually go live within a day, Apple takes longer.

110
00:10:51.943 --> 00:10:56.773
Last quick check. A vendor's documents expired, and they need two weeks to renew.

111
00:10:56.773 --> 00:10:59.218
What should the admin do? Think about it.

112
00:11:03.168 --> 00:11:08.228
The answer: suspend. The vendor goes read only, listings are hidden, and once the

113
00:11:08.228 --> 00:11:11.040
Documents are renewed, the admin re-approves.

114
00:11:13.843 --> 00:11:16.104
Let's recap the whole course in one screen.

115
00:11:16.554 --> 00:11:21.730
Module one. The vendor console has ten sections, and the vendor proposes while the

116
00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:22.677
Admin approves.

117
00:11:23.127 --> 00:11:28.183
Module two. Add S K U, and price and policy change requests with a reason.

118
00:11:28.633 --> 00:11:33.710
Module three. Verify the pickup address in Shiprocket, then approve the warehouse.

119
00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:39.238
Module four. Accept, pick, pack and hand over. And dismiss is not cancel.

120
00:11:39.688 --> 00:11:45.009
Module five. Fifty thousand rupees or more needs an e-way bill, and settlements show

121
00:11:45.009 --> 00:11:45.960
The net payout.

122
00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:51.530
Module six. Suspend, block and delete, and staff permissions with warehouse scope.

123
00:11:53.943 --> 00:11:57.723
That's the end of module 6. You've completed all six modules.

124
00:11:57.723 --> 00:12:00.450
Now take the quiz, and get your certificate.
